{"name":"French Girl","title":"French Girl","revision":227655,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/French_Girl","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The French Girl is a long-standing aesthetic and cultural trope based on a stereotypical image of a chic, sophisticated, and effortlessly \"cool\" Parisian woman. Rather than being an accurate depiction of all French women, it is a highly influential popular culture cliché perpetuated by cinema and fashion media. The aesthetic draws on the concept of nonchalance: a studied carelessness that suggests an innate sense of style without visible effort."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The idealized \"French Girl\" look is often described as \"natural and effortless, achieved with effort.\" It involves a minimalist approach to fashion, typically with a neutral color palette, classic garments like trench coats and Breton striped shirts, and simple accessories. Beauty is similarly understated, emphasizing healthy skin, tousled \"just-woke-up-like-this\" hair, and either a bare face or a single bold element, like red lipstick."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The modern archetype originated in the 1950s and 1960s, heavily influenced by the actresses of French New Wave cinema and the icons of the yé-yé music movement. Figures like Françoise Hardy, Jane Birkin, Jeanne Moreau, and Brigitte Bardot established a look that was both intellectual and alluring, romantic and moody. However, the aesthetic has faced criticism for promoting a narrow and exclusionary standard of beauty that is typically white, thin, and of a specific hair type, failing to represent the diversity of modern France. As noted by critics, the image was largely constructed and popularized by a historically male-dominated media and advertising industry."},{"kind":"heading","text":"History"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The first wave of the French Girl aesthetic began around 1957 with the popularity of the Left Bank \"Beat\" style worn by artists and poets, and lasted to the 1970s."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"A second wave of the French Girl aesthetic began around 2014 with Vogue magazine producing tons of articles on the habits, food, makeup, and clothes loved by French Girls. The articles went beyond images and brand names and many offered \"secret tips\". Emphasis was placed on the effortlessness of French Girl style, in contrast to the more American obsession with perfection achieved through layers of makeup, complicated diets, and extensive workout routines."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"list","text":"Berets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cobblestone streets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crisp white shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fresh flowers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fresh bread"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Clothes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Berets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Silk scarves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black bras"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black tights"},{"kind":"list","text":"Striped T-shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vintage or vintage inspired graphic T-shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"White button-down shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Satin slip dresses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Floral print cotton dresses— usually red with white flowers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather jackets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Skinny jeans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Matchstick pants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loafers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ballet flats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ankle boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ahite sneakers"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Makeup and Hair"},{"kind":"list","text":"Red lipstick"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bob haircut"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shoulder length hair with bangs (the key to French Girl hair is that it looks slightly wind-ruffled)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Natural makeup or no makeup at all"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Stores"},{"kind":"list","text":"Alexandre Vauthier"},{"kind":"list","text":"Amantine"},{"kind":"list","text":"AMI Paris"},{"kind":"list","text":"A.P.C."},{"kind":"list","text":"Atelier Camille"},{"kind":"list","text":"Balzac Paris"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ba&sh"},{"kind":"list","text":"CELINE"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chloé"},{"kind":"list","text":"Claudie Pierlot"},{"kind":"list","text":"Comptoir Des Cotonniers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Éric Bompard"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ernest Leoty"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gaâla"},{"kind":"list","text":"IRO"},{"kind":"list","text":"Isabel Marant"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jacquemus"},{"kind":"list","text":"Keur Paris"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lanvin"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lemaire"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loulou Studio"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maison Michel"},{"kind":"list","text":"MaisonCléo"},{"kind":"list","text":"Maje"},{"kind":"list","text":"Marie Marot"},{"kind":"list","text":"Monoprix"},{"kind":"list","text":"Musier Paris"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pierre Hardy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Princess Tam Tam"},{"kind":"list","text":"Repetto"},{"kind":"list","text":"Roseanna"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rouje"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sandro"},{"kind":"list","text":"Saint James"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sézane"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Kooples"},{"kind":"list","text":"Veja"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sezanne"},{"kind":"list","text":"Zadig & Voltaire"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Food and Drinks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Baguettes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Croissants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dark chocolate"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hot chocolate"},{"kind":"list","text":"Grapes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Café crème"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wine"},{"kind":"list","text":"Champagne"},{"kind":"list","text":"Black tea"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fresh squeezed orange juice"},{"kind":"list","text":"Omelettes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Oysters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ceviche"},{"kind":"list","text":"Carpaccio"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brie cheese"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fresh fruit and vegetables"},{"kind":"list","text":"Grilled salmon"},{"kind":"list","text":"Roasted chicken"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crêpes"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Movies"},{"kind":"list","text":"Amelie (2001)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Betty Blue (1986)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Funny Face (1957)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Television"},{"kind":"list","text":"Emily in Paris (2020-present)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Killing Eve (2018-2022)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"list","text":"Edith Piaf"},{"kind":"list","text":"Carla Bruni"},{"kind":"list","text":"MIKA"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mylène Farmer"},{"kind":"list","text":"Françoise Hardy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Celine Dion"},{"kind":"list","text":"Melody's Echo Chamber"},{"kind":"list","text":"Yé-yé and French Chanson"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Exercise"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Traditionally, the French Girl is famous for being thin despite not utilizing intense workouts, although it is extremely important to note that all bodies are welcome in the French Girl aesthetic! French Girls participate in light, fun activities to stay healthy, such as:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Walking"},{"kind":"list","text":"Riding a bicycle"},{"kind":"list","text":"Yoga"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swimming"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Leisure Activities"},{"kind":"list","text":"Visiting museums and galleries"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hosting dinner parties"},{"kind":"list","text":"Reading/writing poetry"},{"kind":"list","text":"Photography"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shopping in vintage stores"},{"kind":"list","text":"Shopping couture"},{"kind":"list","text":"Painting or sketching from life"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Notable Figures"},{"kind":"heading","text":"1920s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Coco Chanel"},{"kind":"heading","text":"1950s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Audrey Hepburn"},{"kind":"heading","text":"1960s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brigitte Bardot"},{"kind":"list","text":"Françoise Hardy"},{"kind":"heading","text":"1970s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jane Birkin"},{"kind":"heading","text":"1980s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Inès de La Fressange"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vanessa Paradis"},{"kind":"heading","text":"2000s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Audrey Tautou"},{"kind":"heading","text":"2010s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Clémence Poésy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Léa Seydoux"},{"kind":"heading","text":"2020s"},{"kind":"list","text":"Taylor Lashae"},{"kind":"list","text":"Léna Situations"},{"kind":"list","text":"Violette_fr"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fictional Characters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Villanelle | Oksana Astankova in Killing Eve (2018-2022)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Camille in Emily in Paris (2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Madeleine Swann (Léa Seydoux) in Spectre (2015) and No Time To Die (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Amélie Poulain (Audrey Tautou) in Amélie"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vogue French Girl Style article tag"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Blogs"},{"kind":"list","text":"French Girl Daily"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leonce Chenal"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Petite Bijou"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"How to be Parisian Wherever You Are by Anne Berest"},{"kind":"list","text":"Parsian Charm School by Jamie Cat Callan"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Instagram Accounts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jeanne Damas"},{"kind":"list","text":"Violette_fr"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/7a/Jane_birkin.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210703154115","caption":"Jane birkin","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Jane_birkin.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0391-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/e1/Taylor_Lashae.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/1000?cb=20220124164611","caption":"Taylor Lashae's iconic bob hairstyl